{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>But on the tenth day of the month.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it is like 'indeed' (אמנם) — that is to say, on the first day of the seventh month I commanded you that it be the day of judgment, on which you pass before Him as sheep of Maron; but on the tenth of it shall be the Day of Atonements, when I seal the decree of judgment upon you for atonement." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: 'But on the tenth' — אך and רק and מן are terms of restriction (מעוטין). It atones for those who repent but does not atone for those who do not repent. That is to say, even though I ordained for you a day of judgment on the first day of the seventh month, and it applies equally to all, I set aside for you on the tenth of it a day of atonement; and the atonement shall not be equal for everyone but only for those who repent — this is the force of אך."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:55.126397534Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}